// Rule: [T1059.004] CL-UNK-1211 - Mkfifo Bash Nc Reverse Shell
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.004
// Classification: Production candidate
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Production candidate for mkfifo bash nc reverse shell, with evidence boundaries and target-environment validation requirements
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for mkfifo bash nc reverse shell using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: successful C2, impact, or CL-UNK-1211 attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Production candidate - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium | Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Behavior: source-observed Linux named-pipe reverse shell combining
// mkfifo, an interactive Bash shell and Netcat in one command line.
// A match does not prove successful C2, impact, or CL-UNK-1211 attribution.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName in~ ("sh", "bash")
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "mkfifo"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "/tmp/f"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "bash -i"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "nc "
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "|"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountName,
          FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
